<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boers</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Boer</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Boers were the descendants of Dutch-speaking settlers in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, who founded independent republics in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> and Orange Free State in the nineteenth century. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a> of 1899–1902, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> needed around 450,000 troops to defeat about 50,000 Boer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrillas</a>. The war produced the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camp</a> system, which damaged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s international reputation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boers.jpg" alt="Boers" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Rauscher · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boerfamily1886.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
